From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 20:35:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: drain CCU before TTBR0 switch

The A6xx render backend can still have asynchronous work touching color or
depth cache state when the command processor reaches the next context's
page-table update.  If TTBR0 is switched first, those accesses are translated
through the new context and can fault on addresses owned by the old context.

Wait for the old context to become idle, invalidate its CCU state while its
page table is still active, and wait for that operation to complete before
programming the new TTBR0.  Keep the existing A7xx-and-newer timestamp and
context-reset sequence unchanged.

This addresses repeated A640 source=CCU translation faults observed during
KWin context changes on SM8150.

Signed-off-by: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
index 8b3bb2fd433b..4dd0d21394f3 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gpu.c
@@ -241,6 +241,28 @@ static void a6xx_set_pagetable(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu,
 	if (msm_iommu_pagetable_params(to_msm_vm(vm)->mmu, &ttbr, &asid))
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * A6xx can still have asynchronous render-backend work touching the CCU
+	 * when CP reaches the next context's page-table update.  Switching TTBR0
+	 * first makes those accesses run against the new context and turns stale
+	 * color/depth cache lines into translation faults.  Drain the pipeline and
+	 * discard the old context's CCU state while its page table is still active.
+	 * A7xx and newer use the timestamp/context-reset sequence below instead.
+	 */
+	if (adreno_gpu->info->family < ADRENO_7XX_GEN1) {
+		OUT_PKT7(ring, CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE, 0);
+
+		OUT_PKT7(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+		OUT_RING(ring,
+			 CP_EVENT_WRITE_0_EVENT(PC_CCU_INVALIDATE_DEPTH));
+
+		OUT_PKT7(ring, CP_EVENT_WRITE, 1);
+		OUT_RING(ring,
+			 CP_EVENT_WRITE_0_EVENT(PC_CCU_INVALIDATE_COLOR));
+
+		OUT_PKT7(ring, CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE, 0);
+	}
+
 	if (adreno_gpu->info->family >= ADRENO_7XX_GEN1) {
 		/* Wait for previous submit to complete before continuing: */
 		OUT_PKT7(ring, CP_WAIT_TIMESTAMP, 4);
-- 
2.51.0

